        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "EPD_Driver.kicad_sch (Id 3/4): 'C1 0.1uF/16V' between the Display_Power_Switch rail and GND, next to 'C2 1uF/6.3V'."},
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "C2 default: 1 µF/25 V | C1/C5/C7/C8/C9/C10 = 1 µF/25 V | Matches default"}
      ],
      "impact": "The boost-converter input is decoupled with a capacitor ten times smaller than intended (and a lower voltage rating). This raises input-rail ripple/impedance seen by the EPD boost stage and can degrade regulation or stability under display-refresh current bursts, deviating from the intended PDI G1-group behaviour.",
      "confidence": 0.6
    }
  ],
  "summary": "Most of the design matches the specification (regulator topology, EPD parts, barrel-jack battery disconnect, reset wiring, EPD signal mapping). The one clear deviation is C1 on the EPD_Driver sheet, drawn as 0.1 µF/16 V where the spec's directly-sourced component table requires 1 µF/25 V for the boost input decoupling cap."
}

